  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM - Multi Country Humanitarian Assistance -2024/25</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With the support of Global Affairs Canada, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is facilitating access to essential services for crisis affected populations in Bangladesh, in continuation of lifesaving activities contributing towards the alleviation of suffering and maintenance of dignity. Since 2017, IOM has been implementing a multi-sectoral response in the 17 camps under its Area of Responsibility in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar in response to the prolonged displacement of Rohingya refugees from Myanmar and their impact on the host community. This is compounded by the impact of recurring natural hazards in Bangladesh, such as cyclones, monsoons and fire incidents.To address ongoing challenges within this context effectively, IOM is working towards ensuring safer and improved living conditions for Rohingya communities through site development activities, providing lifesaving emergency shelter and non-food items, shelter upgrades and maintenance activities, as well as primary health services and mental health and psychosocial support.</narrative>
  </description>
